      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9013-1",
        "name": "USN-9013-1",
        "description": "Christian Herdtweck discovered that Fetchmail incorrectly handled certain long log messages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Fetchmail to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS. (CVE-2021-36386)  It was discovered that the Fetchmail SMTP client incorrectly handled certain status code messages. An attacker controlling a malicious server could possibly use this issue to cause Fetchmail to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS. (CVE-2025-61962)  Tristan Madani discovered that Fetchmail incorrectly handled certain NTLM authentication challenges. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Fetchmail to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. The default compiler options for affected releases should reduce the vulnerability to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94184)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2021-36386",
          "CVE-2025-61962",
          "CVE-2026-94184"
        ]
      },
      "timestamp": "2026-11-09T17:17:55Z",
